// Per-term Chu Nom display order.
//
// The base and supplemental dictionary layers extend a term's candidate list, while local
// entries lead those lower-priority candidates. Rows here run last and move the listed
// variants to the very front, in the order given; everything else keeps its relative order
// behind them. A variant the dictionaries never listed is inserted rather than ignored, so
// a row can pin as well as reorder.
//
// A dictionary row can hold several renderings as one grouped cell ("巴|芭|𠀧|爸"). The
// build preserves that source row unchanged, but emits a separate exact row in front when a
// preferred rendering is otherwise trapped inside the group. Thus every consumer displays
// the local preference first without rewriting the grouped dictionary fact.
//
// `vi` is the key (normalized the same way every term in this repository is) and rows are
// upserts: one row per term. Usually authored from the book-translator reader's
// "Set Chu Nom order" action; hand edits and these comments are preserved by that writer.
//
// Consumed by scripts/build-nom-userscript.js, scripts/build-popupdict-userscript.js,
// scripts/build-extension-vnedict-json.js and the reader's scripts/reader/nom_order.py.
[
  // ba: 𠀧 is the ordinary Nom numeral; 巴 is a phonetic borrowing that happened to be
  // listed first.
  { "vi": "ba", "nom": ["𠀧"] },
  {"vi": "Linh", "nom": ["灵"]},
  {"vi": "cần", "nom": ["𥵚"]},
